  (3, 'english', 'all', 'Writing transcription (spelling)', 'write from memory simple sentences, dictated by the teacher, that include words and punctuation taught so far', 'National curriculum in England: English programmes of study, updated 16 July 2014, years 3 and 4', true, null, 180),
  (3, 'english', 'all', 'Writing transcription (handwriting)', 'use the diagonal and horizontal strokes that are needed to join letters and understand which letters, when adjacent to one another, are best left unjoined', 'National curriculum in England: English programmes of study, updated 16 July 2014, years 3 and 4', true, null, 190),
  (3, 'english', 'all', 'Writing transcription (handwriting)', 'increase the legibility, consistency and quality of their handwriting, [for example, by ensuring that the downstrokes of letters are parallel and equidistant, and that lines of writing are spaced sufficiently so that the ascenders and descenders of letters do not touch]', 'National curriculum in England: English programmes of study, updated 16 July 2014, years 3 and 4', true, null, 200),
  (3, 'english', 'all', 'Writing composition', 'plan their writing by: discussing writing similar to that which they are planning to write in order to understand and learn from its structure, vocabulary and grammar' || chr(59) || ' discussing and recording ideas', 'National curriculum in England: English programmes of study, updated 16 July 2014, years 3 and 4', true, null, 210),
  (3, 'english', 'all', 'Writing composition', 'draft and write by: composing and rehearsing sentences orally (including dialogue), progressively building a varied and rich vocabulary and an increasing range of sentence structures English appendix 2' || chr(59) || ' organising paragraphs around a theme' || chr(59) || ' in narratives, creating settings, characters and plot' || chr(59) || ' in non-narrative material, using simple organisational devices [for example, headings and sub-headings]', 'National curriculum in England: English programmes of study, updated 16 July 2014, years 3 and 4', true, null, 220),
  (3, 'english', 'all', 'Writing composition', 'evaluate and edit by: assessing the effectiveness of their own and others'' writing and suggesting improvements' || chr(59) || ' proposing changes to grammar and vocabulary to improve consistency, including the accurate use of pronouns in sentences', 'National curriculum in England: English programmes of study, updated 16 July 2014, years 3 and 4', true, null, 230),
  (3, 'english', 'all', 'Writing composition', 'proofread for spelling and punctuation errors', 'National curriculum in England: English programmes of study, updated 16 July 2014, years 3 and 4', true, null, 240),
  (3, 'english', 'all', 'Writing composition', 'read their own writing aloud to a group or the whole class, using appropriate intonation and controlling the tone and volume so that the meaning is clear', 'National curriculum in England: English programmes of study, updated 16 July 2014, years 3 and 4', true, null, 250),
  (3, 'english', 'all', 'Writing vocabulary grammar and punctuation', 'develop their understanding of the concepts set out in English appendix 2 by: extending the range of sentences with more than one clause by using a wider range of conjunctions, including: when, if, because, although' || chr(59) || ' using the present perfect form of verbs in contrast to the past tense' || chr(59) || ' choosing nouns or pronouns appropriately for clarity and cohesion and to avoid repetition' || chr(59) || ' using conjunctions, adverbs and prepositions to express time and cause' || chr(59) || ' using fronted adverbials' || chr(59) || ' learning the grammar for years 3 and 4 in [English appendix 2]', 'National curriculum in England: English programmes of study, updated 16 July 2014, years 3 and 4', true, null, 260),
  (3, 'english', 'all', 'Writing vocabulary grammar and punctuation', 'indicate grammatical and other features by: using commas after fronted adverbials' || chr(59) || ' indicating possession by using the possessive apostrophe with plural nouns' || chr(59) || ' using and punctuating direct speech', 'National curriculum in England: English programmes of study, updated 16 July 2014, years 3 and 4', true, null, 270),
